A. PRECOMPUTATION PIPELINE IMPLEMENTED
--------------------------------------

Developed a full metric precomputation loop across
snapshots (0–799):

For each snapshot:
    • Loaded MW_###.txt and M31_###.txt
    • Combined halo particle arrays
    • Applied COM centering using MW.COMdefine
    • Computed full 3D inertia tensor
    • Diagonalized tensor (numpy.linalg.eigh)
    • Extracted principal axes (a ≥ b ≥ c)
    • Computed ellipsoidal volume:
            V_ellipsoid = (4/3)πabc
    • Computed convex hull volume via scipy.spatial.ConvexHull
    • Calculated:
            b/a
            c/a
            Volume inflation = V_hull / V_ellipsoid

Stored all results in NumPy arrays for efficient reuse
during rendering.

Design principle:
    Physics computed once.
    Rendering performs zero heavy calculations.

